⇒ returns a **pa**; `pin=1` means "never evict" (kernel stacks); `pgtable=NULL` is legal and must be tolerated by `selete_page`/`write_to_sd`.

### `free_user_page` — `init/main.c:211` (idle-loop reaper — this defines `do_exit`'s contract)
```c
    while (1){
        disable_preempt();
        list_node_t* clean_node = kernel_pcb[0].wait_list.next;
        while(clean_node != &kernel_pcb[0].wait_list){
            pcb_t *clean_pcb = list_entry(clean_node, pcb_t, list);
            // release pcb
            clean_pcb->status = TASK_EXITED;
            clean_pcb->pid = -1;
            // release kernel stack
            free_user_page(kva2pa(clean_pcb->kernel_stack_base - PAGE_SIZE));

            clean_node = clean_node->next;
            list_del(clean_node->prev);
        }

        enable_preempt();
        __asm__ __volatile__("wfi\n\r":::);
    }
```
⇒ `do_exit` (AUTO_CLEANUP mode) must park the dying PCB's `list` node on `kernel_pcb[0].wait_list`; core 0's idle loop frees the kernel stack and recycles the slot. `kernel_stack_base` is the **top** kva of a one-page kernel stack.

