plus `kernel_pcb[0..1]` init with `.pgdir = (PTE*)PGDIR_PA`, `.mask = 1`/`2`, `.cpu_id = 0`/`1`, `.status = TASK_RUNNING`, and finally `current_running[0] = &kernel_pcb[0]; current_running[1] = &kernel_pcb[1];`. Only `kernel_pcb[0].wait_list` and `pcb[0].wait_list` are initialized here — `do_exec` must `init_list_head(&pcb[i].wait_list)` for every new task.

