## 8. Consolidated checklist of what each stub must do

**mm.c**
| function | returns | must do |
|---|---|---|
| `alloc_user_page(pin,pgtable)` | pa | scan `user_page[]` for `!valid`; if none, `pa = selete_page(); write_to_sd(pa);` then reuse it. Set `valid=1`, `pin`, `pgtable`. Zero the frame via `pa2kva`. |
| `selete_page()` | pa | NRU/second-chance over `user_page[]`, skipping `pin` and `pgtable==NULL`; clear `_PAGE_ACCESSED` while sweeping. |
| `write_to_sd(pa)` | — | find free `disk_page[]` slot i; `sbi_sd_write(pa, 8, SWAP_BEGIN + i*8)`; rewrite `*user_page[pa2num(pa)].pgtable` to the swapped-out encoding; `local_flush_tlb_all()`; `free_user_page(pa)`. |
| `init_page_table()` | pa (`PTE*`) | `alloc_pgdir_page()`; copy boot entry `[0x101]`; map 3 code pages `0x10000..0x13000` and the stack page `USER_STACK_ADDR-PAGE_SIZE`, allocating intermediate tables with `alloc_pgdir_page()` and frames with `alloc_user_page(0, &leaf_pte)`; leaves need `V|R|W|X|U|A|D`. |
| `free_process_user_page(pgdir)` | — | walk all 512×512×512 *present* user entries (VPN2 < 0x100), `free_user_page(get_pa(pte))` for leaves, `free_pgdir_page` for the intermediate tables and the root; also release any `disk_page[]` slots and decrement `shm_page[].count`. |
| `shm_page_get(key)` | user va | find/create `shm_page[key % SHM_PAGE_NUM]` (or by key search); allocate the frame with `alloc_user_page(1, NULL)` on first use; `count++`; map it into the first free VA in `0x1000..0x10000` of the caller's pgdir; return that VA (0 on failure). |
| `shm_page_dt(addr)` | — | zero the leaf PTE for `addr`, `local_flush_tlb_all()`, `count--`, `free_user_page(pa)` when it hits 0. |
| `handle_page_fault(regs,stval,cause)` | — | walk `current_running[cpu_id]->pgdir` for `stval`; create missing levels; if the leaf is swapped (`_PAGE_SOFT`) read it back from the SD; else `alloc_user_page(0,&leaf)`; set `V|R|W|X|U|A|D`; flush. |

**sched.c**
| function | must do |
|---|---|
| `scheduler()` | re-queue prev if `status==TASK_RUNNING` and it is not `&kernel_pcb[cpu_id]` (set `ready_tick`); pick via `max_priority_node()` honoring `mask & (1<<cpu_id)`; fall back to `&kernel_pcb[cpu_id]`; `list_del` the chosen node; set `status/cpu_id`; write `current_running[cpu_id]` **and** `current_cpu_running`; restore `screen_cursor_x/y[cpu_id]`; `set_satp(SATP_MODE_SV39, 0, ((uintptr_t)next->pgdir)>>NORMAL_PAGE_SHIFT); local_flush_tlb_all();` |
| `do_exec()` | `enable_sum()` to read `file_name`/`argv`; `get_elf_file` (0 ⇒ `-1`); free PCB slot (`pid==-1`, none ⇒ `0`); `free_page_num()` check (⇒ `-2`); `init_page_table()`; `load_elf(..., get_kva_of)`; kernel stack via `alloc_user_page(1,NULL)`; copy argv strings into the child's stack page through `pa2kva(get_pa(...))`; `init_pcb_stack` then patch `regs[10]=argc, regs[11]=child_argv_va`; init `wait_list`, `binsem_num`, `mask=3`, `mode`, `status=TASK_READY`, `ready_tick`, `pid = process_id++`; `list_add_tail(&pcb[i].list,&ready_queue)`; return the pid. |
| `do_exit()` | release held binsems (`binsem_id[0..binsem_num)`), `do_unblock` everyone on `current->wait_list`, `list_del(&current->timer.list)`, `free_process_user_page(pgdir)` + free the pgdir pages, then either `status=TASK_ZOMBIE` (ENTER_ZOMBIE_ON_EXIT) or `list_add_tail(&current->list, &kernel_pcb[0].wait_list)` for the reaper (AUTO_CLEANUP_ON_EXIT); finally `scheduler()`. |
| `do_kill(pid)` | return 0 if no such pid (shell prints "Task Does Not Exist"), else do the `do_exit` teardown on that PCB from the outside (it may be BLOCKED, READY, or RUNNING on the other core) and return non-zero. Note the shell refuses to kill pid 0/1 itself. |
| `do_waitpid(pid,...,regs)` | find the target; if gone/zombie, reap and return; else `do_block(&current->list, &target->wait_list)`, `regs->sepc -= 4` (undo `handle_syscall`'s `+= 4` so the `ecall` retries after wakeup), `scheduler()`. |
| `max_priority_node()` | see the P2b reference above, plus the affinity filter. |

**Most likely footguns:** forgetting `current_cpu_running` in `scheduler()` (silent no-op switch); passing a kva to `sbi_sd_*`; forgetting `enable_sum()` around user pointers in `do_exec` (the other syscalls already do it); building a process pgdir without entry `[0x101]` (instant fault the moment you `sret`... actually the moment the next trap enters the kernel); and mapping user leaves without `_PAGE_USER`.
